    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** (70.72) and **Jackson Merrill** (70.04) leading the offensive charge. **Gunnar Henderson** remains a premier start against Gausman; while the pitcher's skill is a limiting factor, the 14% platoon boost and his elite ability to exploit Gausman\u2019s slow delivery for stolen base opportunities make him the engine of our lineup. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a strong BvP history (32 PA) against Brazob\u00e1n. Despite some defensive headwinds from an elite hold SP, his dynamic platoon advantage cements him as a high-ceiling option capable of delivering across all five categories. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (64.55) and **Kyle Tucker** (64.36) provide the necessary stability, with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** capitalizing on a favorable park factor despite facing a respectable arm in Baz.\n\nStrategic platoon optimization is a theme today, particularly with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (63.63), whose 14% platoon boost against Soroka pushes him into elite territory. Conversely, the most difficult bench decision involved **Nasim Nunez**, who posted a 46.44 efficiency score. While his speed profile is highly coveted, the projected #8 spot in the lineup proved too punitive for our optimizer to justify over the higher-upside profiles like **Liam Hicks** or **Miguel Vargas**. We are also exercising caution with **Miguel Andujar** (40.44), who sits right on the edge of our efficiency floor; his negative platoon variance against Brazob\u00e1n makes him a candidate to be swapped if official lineups shift his position downward.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for several key players. Because we rely on assumed batting positions, any drop in the order for **Curtis Mead**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, or **Andy Pages** would necessitate a recalculation of their daily efficiency scores. **Andy Pages** faces additional pressure today due to an elite catcher matchup, which suppresses his stolen base floor, while **Sam Antonacci** remains a solid play (56.83) thanks to a favorable park factor and a strong xwOBA. We are holding **Coby Mayo** and **Nolan Schanuel** on the bench for today; while they possess raw power, their matchup metrics against Gausman and Sheehan, respectively, failed to clear the threshold required to displace our current starters.",
